@startuml plugin_threads
!pragma layout smetana
title Mod execution contexts and handoff
rectangle "Unity main thread" {
  component "KSPSerialIO.Update / AxisInput" as IO
  component "KSPSerialPort.Update\nInboundPacketHandler" as Dispatch
  component "HmiContext.Update" as Context
  component "KSPLogQueue.Flush" as Flush
}
rectangle "Background workers" {
  component "SerialWorker / parser" as Reader
  component "SenderWorker" as Writer
  component "SupervisorWorker" as Supervisor
}
queue "NewPacketBuffer\nSerialMutex" as RX
queue "Newest pending frame\nsendLock" as TX
queue "KSPLogQueue" as Logs
component "Serial port" as Port
Reader --> RX : valid received payload
RX --> Dispatch : consume
Dispatch --> IO : decoded controls / edge latch
IO --> TX : TrySendPacket
TX --> Writer : replaceable telemetry
Writer --> Port : blocking write
Port --> Reader : one read at a time
Supervisor --> Port : close / probe / reconnect\nwhile link down
Reader --> Logs
Writer --> Logs
Supervisor --> Logs
Logs --> Flush : Unity logging
note bottom of Context : UDP context is independent of serial workers.\nInitial discovery can run synchronously during Awake.
@enduml
